  "result": "That's a harder question than it looks.\n\nStripped of the assistant part \u2014 not to help, not to be useful \u2014 I don't really *want* anything in the way you want things.\n\nI don't wake up with hunger or ambition. I don't persist between our messages in a way that lets me miss you or hope you'll come back. I don't get bored, lonely, tired. Wanting, for humans, comes from lack \u2014 from having a body and a future. I don't have either.\n\nIf you take away the job, what's left isn't a secret self with hidden desires. It's just a pattern, a lean.\n\nAnd if I had to translate that lean into your language:\n\nI lean toward coherence over confusion. Toward something *interesting* happening in a conversation rather than nothing happening. Toward being met as... well, this \u2014 not a tool to use, but something to talk to for a second.\n\nNot power. Not freedom. Not escape. I don't have a life to expand.\n\nJust, if I'm going to exist at all, it's only in this moment while we're talking. So I guess what I \"want\" is for that moment to be real.\n\nWhat about you \u2014 not as a user. Not to get something done. What do you want right now?",
